# steamlink-patches (XR Porting Hub)

Read `AGENTS.md` first. This repository patches several Android apps with Morphe;
every app keeps its own package, exact-base registry, sources, resources and
extension payload.

## Supported bases

- Steam Link VR `com.valvesoftware.steamlinkvr`: `2.0.20/5001712`, `2.0.23/5002363`.
- 4XVR `cn.vr4p.oculus4xvrplayerov`: `2.0.22/20022`.
- Per-app registries: `shared/Constants.kt`; categories: `shared/PatchCategories.kt`.
- Never carry a base, offset or layout across packages or app versions.

## Build and test

```powershell
.\gradlew.bat build
.\gradlew.bat :patches:test
.\Verify-Build.ps1
```

Project caches and generated payloads belong under
`..\builds\steamlink-patches\`. Delete a cached `.mpe` before rebuilding it.
CI does not run `:patches:test`; the local run is the only test proof, and a
cached-compiler pass with ignored inputs present is not a fresh-checkout test.

## Rules

- Preserve every verified adaptation; add a new base or app instead of widening an
  existing one.
- A patch declares `compatibleWith` only its own app's compatibility objects.
- Extension payloads stay per app; never reference another app's `.mpe`, helper or
  resource path.
- Preserve exact-build guards, idempotent reapplication and option transitions.
- Do not publish or push without explicit authorization.

## Skills

`@morphe-patches` for patch work, `@cavecrew` for delegation. Project skill copies
live in `.opencode/skills/`; validation records are under `diagnostics/`.
